  "disposition": [
    "Retain all native errors. Reader and psd-tools stop after the expected output width and accept productive/incomplete suffixes. This is not proof of strict packet validity.",
    "ImageMagick also rejects the double-no-op control, so its rejection cannot be adopted indiscriminately as a validity contract. Investigate input-size checks separately from PackBits packet checks.",
    "Pillow direct PSD output reverses bitmap polarity relative to reader, psd-tools and successful ImageMagick controls; it does not open these PSBs. Do not change reader pixels to its output.",
    "Next: audit the Adobe composite-row rule and full PackBits consumption, add multichannel/depth/row controls, and separate permitted padding/no-ops from incomplete packets before a fix."
  ]
